###############################################################################
# Q11 -- Computational resources
###############################################################################

# The paper reports no training-cost or inference-cost figures.

###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - Table I gives the errors on one DFT-optimised structure per molecule ('energy error' and 'mean errors' of forces), not test-set statistics; they are encoded as MAE with that stated in the labels. The test-set RMSEs of the paper are in the Supporting Information. Charge errors (in 10^-3 e) have no MetricProperty.
# - '3G-HDNNP (unscaled)' and '(scaled)' are two treatments of the predicted charges of one 3G model and are encoded as two results on it.
# - The three other benchmark systems (Ag3 +/- clusters, Na8/9Cl8+ clusters, Au2 on doped and undoped MgO(001); 5000, 5000 and about 10,000 reference points) are not encoded: their errors are in figures or in the SI. These data sets are the ones later reused by ji2025 and ji2026.
# - Symmetry-function parameters are in the SI (cutoffs of 8-10 Bohr depending on the system; the 4.23 A stated for C10H2 is encoded). The screening radii of the short-range electrostatics and the Gaussian charge widths are not encoded.
# - 2G-HDNNP is encoded under the registry method entity:HDNNP; 3G and 4G are separate registry methods because the functional form differs (METHODS.md rule 3).
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: crossref).
